<title>Pigmented Villonodular Synovitis: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0403-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Suspected pigmented villonodular synovitis (PVNS): chronic&#x002F;recurrent monoarticular joint pain, swelling, and stiffness (especially in the knee); mechanical symptoms of mass effect; joint effusion with diffuse tenderness and loss of motion.</label>
<path target="cell-2"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Plain radiographs typical of PVNS? (Soft tissue swelling, periarticular bone erosions, subchondral cysts.)</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>MRI results typical of PVNS? (Effusion, low signal intensity on T1- and T2-weighted images, hyperplastic synovium, bony erosions.)</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Consider other diagnoses.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Synovial biopsy typical for PVNS? (Proliferative sheets of mononuclear cells within the synovium, presence of hemosiderin.)</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Synovectomy: Open versus arthroscopic, with or without adjuvant therapy.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
<algorithm id="fig002">
<meta>
<id>403</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title>Pigmented Villonodular Synovitis: Treatment.</title>
<graphic href="eee0403-w0002.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-7">
<label>Type of PVNS of the knee.</label>
<path target="cell-9">Localized nodular</path>
<path target="cell-8">Diffuse villous</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-8">
<label>Primary or recurrent?</label>
<path target="cell-11">Primary</path>
<path target="cell-10">Recurrent</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-10">
<label>Articular surface findings?</label>
<path target="cell-13">Articular surfaces preserved</path>
<path target="cell-12">Significant articular degeneration</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>Arthrodesis or total knee replacement.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Repeat total synovectomy; consider adjuvant therapy.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Arthroscopic or open total synovectomy.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-9">
<label>Site</label>
<path target="cell-15">Extra-articular</path>
<path target="cell-14">Intra-articular</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-14">
<label>Arthroscopic excision.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-15">
<label>Open excision.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Adapted from Kramer DE, Frassica FJ, Frassica DA, Cosgarea AJ. Pigmented villonodular synovitis of the knee: diagnosis and treatment. <em>J Knee Surg</em> 2009 Jul;<strong>22</strong>(3):243-254.<xref ref="pubmed19634729" resource="acc007" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
